IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 8 -- Terms and references in Acts, third group (ss 35B to 36).
-- Section 35B says what a reference to a provision "designated by a number" (for example "section 10", "part 1", "paragraph (a)") refers to,
-- by where the reference occurs: the body of the Act, the preamble, a schedule or an appendix.

§ `Part 8 -- Terms and references in Acts (ss 35B to 36)`

§§ `s 35B -- References to provisions designated by number without mentioning another Act`

DECLARE `Part of an Act` IS ONE OF
    `the preamble`
    `a schedule`
    `an appendix`
    `any other part of the Act`

-- src:719 | In this section—
-- src:720 | body of the Act means the Act apart from any preamble, schedule or appendix of the Act.
@ref s 35B(1), definition body of the Act (src:719-720)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the part is in the body of the Act (s 35B(1), definition body of the Act)` IS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the preamble` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a schedule` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an appendix` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `any other part of the Act` THEN JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Candidate provision unit` IS ONE OF
    `the body of the Act`
    `the preamble`
    `a schedule`
    `an appendix`
    `a chapter`
    `a part`
    `a division`
    `a subdivision`
    `a section`
    `a subsection`
    `a paragraph`
    `a subparagraph`
    `a sub-subparagraph`
    `another provision of the body of the Act or a schedule or appendix of the Act`
    `a provision of a preamble of the Act`
    `something that is none of these`

-- "provision unit means" (a) to (d): a closed list.
-- src:721 | provision unit means—
-- src:722 | (a) the body of the Act or the preamble, a schedule or appendix of the Act; or
-- src:723 | (b) a chapter, part, division, subdivision, section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or sub-subparagraph of the body of the Act or a schedule or appendix of the Act; or
-- src:724 | (c) another provision of the body of the Act or a schedule or appendix of the Act; or
-- src:725 | (d) a provision of a preamble of the Act.
@ref s 35B(1), definition provision unit (src:721-725)
GIVEN unit IS A `Candidate provision unit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unit is a provision unit (s 35B(1), definition provision unit)` IS
    CONSIDER unit
    WHEN `something that is none of these` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:727 | This section explains the meaning of a reference in an Act (the Act concerned) to a provision, designated by a number, that does not mention another Act.
@ref s 35B(2) (src:727-727)
GIVEN `the reference is to a provision designated by a number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference does not mention another Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35B explains the meaning of the reference (s 35B(2))` IS
    IF `the reference is to a provision designated by a number` AND `the reference does not mention another Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Where a reference to a provision occurs` IS ONE OF
    `in the body of the Act`
    `in the preamble`
    `in a schedule`
    `in an appendix`

DECLARE `What a reference to a provision designated by a number refers to` IS ONE OF
    `the provision the reference itself indicates`
    `the provision, designated by the number, of the body of the Act concerned`
    `the provision, designated by the number, of the schedule, appendix or preamble where the reference occurs`
    `the provision, designated by the number, of the next larger, appropriate provision unit where the reference occurs`

-- (3) and (4): the reference also mentions the Act or a larger provision unit: the reference itself indicates the provision;
-- but a reference in a schedule or appendix with the words "of the Act" is to the provision of the body of the Act.
-- (5): in the body of an Act: the provision of the body of the Act, or, if there are 2 such provisions, of the next larger, appropriate provision unit where the reference occurs.
-- (6): in the preamble, schedule or appendix, to a provision that does not occur there: the provision of the body of the Act.
-- (7): in the preamble, schedule or appendix, to a provision that does occur there: the provision of the schedule, appendix or preamble, or, if there are 2 such provisions, of the next larger, appropriate unit.
-- src:734 | If a reference in an Act to a provision also mentions the Act or a larger provision unit of the Act, the reference itself indicates the provision of the Act to which it refers.
@ref s 35B(3) (src:734-734)
-- src:739 | (4) For subsection (3), a reference in a schedule or appendix of an Act to a provision, designated by a number, together with the words ‘of the Act’ is a reference to the provision, designated by the number, of the body of the Act concerned.
@ref s 35B(4) (src:739-739)
-- src:743 | If—
-- src:744 | (a) the reference is in the body of an Act; and
-- src:745 | (b) subsection (4) does not apply to the reference;
-- src:746 | the reference is a reference to the provision, designated by the number, of the body of the Act or, if there are 2 such provisions, the provision, designated by the number, of the next larger, appropriate provision unit where the reference occurs.
@ref s 35B(5) (src:743-746)
-- src:761 | If—
-- src:762 | (a) the reference is in the preamble or a schedule or appendix of an Act; and
-- src:763 | (b) subsection (4) does not apply to the reference; and
-- src:764 | (c) the reference is a reference to a provision that does not occur in the preamble, schedule or appendix;
-- src:765 | the reference is a reference to the provision, designated by the number, of the body of the Act.
@ref s 35B(6) (src:761-765)
-- src:769 | (7) If—
-- src:770 | (a) the reference is in the preamble or a schedule or appendix of an Act; and
-- src:771 | (b) subsection (4) does not apply to the reference; and
-- src:772 | (c) the reference is a reference to a provision that does occur in the preamble, schedule or appendix;
-- src:773 | the reference is a reference to the provision designated by the number, of the schedule, appendix or preamble or, if there are 2 such provisions, the provision, designated by the number, of the next larger, appropriate provision unit where the reference occurs.
@ref s 35B(7) (src:769-773)
GIVEN place IS A `Where a reference to a provision occurs`
      `the reference also mentions the Act or a larger provision unit of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference, in a schedule or appendix, has the words of the Act with the number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision referred to occurs in the preamble, schedule or appendix where the reference occurs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are 2 such provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What a reference to a provision designated by a number refers to`
DECIDE `what a reference to a provision designated by a number refers to (s 35B(3) to (7))` IS
    IF `the reference also mentions the Act or a larger provision unit of the Act`
    THEN CONSIDER place
        WHEN `in a schedule` THEN IF `the reference, in a schedule or appendix, has the words of the Act with the number` THEN `the provision, designated by the number, of the body of the Act concerned` ELSE `the provision the reference itself indicates`
        WHEN `in an appendix` THEN IF `the reference, in a schedule or appendix, has the words of the Act with the number` THEN `the provision, designated by the number, of the body of the Act concerned` ELSE `the provision the reference itself indicates`
        OTHERWISE `the provision the reference itself indicates`
    ELSE CONSIDER place
        WHEN `in the body of the Act` THEN
            IF `there are 2 such provisions`
            THEN `the provision, designated by the number, of the next larger, appropriate provision unit where the reference occurs`
            ELSE `the provision, designated by the number, of the body of the Act concerned`
        OTHERWISE
            IF NOT `the provision referred to occurs in the preamble, schedule or appendix where the reference occurs`
            THEN `the provision, designated by the number, of the body of the Act concerned`
            ELSE IF `there are 2 such provisions`
                 THEN `the provision, designated by the number, of the next larger, appropriate provision unit where the reference occurs`
                 ELSE `the provision, designated by the number, of the schedule, appendix or preamble where the reference occurs`

§§ `s 35C and s 35CA -- Headings part of provision etc.`

-- src:784 | (1) The heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, section, subsection, schedule or another provision of an Act forms part of the provision to which it is a heading.
@ref s 35C(1) (src:784-784)
GIVEN `it is the heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, section, subsection, schedule or another provision of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the heading forms part of the provision to which it is a heading (s 35C(1))` IS
    IF `it is the heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, section, subsection, schedule or another provision of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): "unless the example relates to a different provision"
-- FORK once the example relates to a different provision: NOTHING (s 35C(2) no longer answers) || JUST FALSE
-- src:785 | (2) An example of the operation of a provision of an Act at the end of the provision is part of the provision unless the example relates to a different provision.
-- src:786 | Example of subsection (2)—
-- src:787 | This example forms part of subsection (2) and an amendment omitting subsection (2) would omit this example.
@ref s 35C(2) (src:785-787)
GIVEN `it is an example of the operation of a provision of an Act at the end of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the example relates to a different provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the example is part of the provision (s 35C(2))` IS
    IF `it is an example of the operation of a provision of an Act at the end of the provision` AND (NOT `the example relates to a different provision`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:788 | (3) A note to a provision of an Act at the end of the provision is part of the provision unless the note relates to a different provision.
@ref s 35C(3) (src:788-788)
GIVEN `it is a note to a provision of an Act at the end of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note relates to a different provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the note is part of the provision (s 35C(3))` IS
    IF `it is a note to a provision of an Act at the end of the provision` AND (NOT `the note relates to a different provision`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `What a penalty at the end of a subsection is part of` IS ONE OF
    `the subsection`
    `the section`

-- src:789 | (4) A penalty at the end of a subsection of an Act—
-- src:790 | (a) is part of the subsection unless the penalty relates to other subsections of the section; or
-- src:791 | (b) in any other case—is part of the section.
@ref s 35C(4) (src:789-791)
GIVEN `it is a penalty at the end of a subsection of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty relates to other subsections of the section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `What a penalty at the end of a subsection is part of`
DECIDE `what a penalty at the end of a subsection is part of (s 35C(4))` IS
    IF NOT `it is a penalty at the end of a subsection of an Act`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the penalty relates to other subsections of the section` THEN JUST `the section` ELSE JUST `the subsection`

-- src:792 | (5) A penalty at the end of a section of an Act that is not divided into subsections is part of the section.
@ref s 35C(5) (src:792-792)
GIVEN `it is a penalty at the end of a section of an Act that is not divided into subsections` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the penalty is part of the section (s 35C(5))` IS
    IF `it is a penalty at the end of a section of an Act that is not divided into subsections` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Where a connecting word is` IS ONE OF
    `at the end of a paragraph, subparagraph, sub-subparagraph or another provision`
    `between paragraphs, subparagraphs, sub-subparagraphs or other provisions`
    `elsewhere`

DECLARE `Provision a connecting word forms part of` IS ONE OF
    `the provision concerned`
    `the first of the provisions`

-- src:793 | (6) The word ‘and’, ‘or’ or ‘but’, or a similar word, at the end of a paragraph, subparagraph, sub-subparagraph or another provision of an Act forms part of the provision concerned.
@ref s 35C(6) (src:793-793)
-- src:794 | (7) The word ‘and’, ‘or’ or ‘but’, or a similar word, between paragraphs, subparagraphs, sub-subparagraphs or other provisions of an Act forms part of the first of the provisions.
@ref s 35C(7) (src:794-794)
GIVEN `the word is and, or or but, or a similar word` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `Where a connecting word is`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Provision a connecting word forms part of`
DECIDE `what the connecting word forms part of (s 35C(6) and (7))` IS
    IF NOT `the word is and, or or but, or a similar word`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER place
        WHEN `at the end of a paragraph, subparagraph, sub-subparagraph or another provision` THEN JUST `the provision concerned`
        WHEN `between paragraphs, subparagraphs, sub-subparagraphs or other provisions` THEN JUST `the first of the provisions`
        WHEN `elsewhere` THEN NOTHING

-- src:795 | (8) A provision reference associated with a heading to a schedule is part of the heading.
@ref s 35C(8) (src:795-795)
GIVEN `it is a provision reference associated with a heading to a schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision reference is part of the heading (s 35C(8))` IS
    IF `it is a provision reference associated with a heading to a schedule` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:796 | Note—
-- src:797 | The provision referred to is the authorising provision or another provision relevant to the schedule.
@ref s 35C(8), note (src:796-797)
GIVEN `it is the authorising provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another provision relevant to the schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision referred to by the provision reference is the authorising provision or another provision relevant to the schedule (s 35C(8), note)` IS
    JUST (`it is the authorising provision` OR `it is another provision relevant to the schedule`)

-- src:799 | In an Act, a penalty, example or note (end item) is taken to be at the end of a provision even if there is another end item also at the end of the provision.
@ref s 35CA (src:799-799)
GIVEN `it is a penalty, example or note (end item) at the end of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another end item is also at the end of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the end item is taken to be at the end of the provision (s 35CA)` IS
    IF `it is a penalty, example or note (end item) at the end of a provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 35D to 36 -- inclusive references, instruments made under the Act, schedule 1`

-- s 35D: a reference to a part of a law is a reference to (a) the provision forming the beginning, (b) the end, (c) any provision between.
-- Provisions are placed on a line by position; a heading between two sections has a position between theirs.
-- src:801 | In an Act, a reference to a part of a law (including the Act) is a reference to the following—
-- src:802 | (a) the provision of the law that forms the beginning of the part;
-- src:803 | (b) the provision of the law that forms the end of the part;
-- src:804 | (c) any provision of the law between the beginning and end of the part.
@ref s 35D (src:801-804)
GIVEN `the position of the provision` IS A NUMBER
      `the position of the provision that forms the beginning of the part` IS A NUMBER
      `the position of the provision that forms the end of the part` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is within a reference to a part of a law (s 35D)` IS
    JUST (   `the position of the provision` AT LEAST `the position of the provision that forms the beginning of the part`
         AND `the position of the provision` AT MOST `the position of the provision that forms the end of the part`)

-- src:810 | In an Act, a reference to a type of statutory instrument is a reference to an instrument of that type made or in force under the Act in which the reference is used.
@ref s 35E (src:810-810)
GIVEN `the instrument is of the type referred to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is made or in force under the Act in which the reference is used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is the instrument a reference to a type of statutory instrument is a reference to (s 35E)` IS
    JUST (`the instrument is of the type referred to` AND `the instrument is made or in force under the Act in which the reference is used`)

-- src:814 | (1) In an Act, a term defined in schedule 1 has the meaning stated in that schedule.
@ref s 36(1) (src:814-814)
GIVEN `the term is defined in schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term has the meaning stated in schedule 1 in an Act (s 36(1))` IS
    IF `the term is defined in schedule 1` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:815 | (2) In an Act, a reference to schedule 1 of this Act includes, if the context permits, a reference to this section.
@ref s 36(2) (src:815-815)
GIVEN `the context permits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to schedule 1 of this Act includes a reference to s 36 (s 36(2))` IS
    IF `the context permits` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
